WEBVTT

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.690
Blanc et Noir.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.240
S-So cute!

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.240
Newbie!

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:17.700
Rending Gale Blade!

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.450
Evade, newbie!

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.950
S-S-S-Snip!

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.000
Sni—

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.580
Petits Ciseaux!

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.090
Balles Pastels!

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.720
Storm!

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.190
Snip, snip, snip.

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.500
Snippity snip!

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.790
Huh? This is how you respond?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.200
This is kind of different.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:12.300
Maybe it's not what I thought.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.260
Wh-What the...

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.970
You idiot!

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.010
Tachikawa Station North Exit

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.010
You've got to be kidding me!

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.930
Human lives are at stake!

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:46.180
Do you understand what 
your intervention means?

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.980
I guess we go back the normal way?

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.490
C'mon, give up your seat.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.340
Senpai, maybe everyone's tired.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.050
Huh?

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.620
Someone might feel awful, 
but can't skip work.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.970
Someone might be sick, too.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.170
We've leased this thirteenth floor.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.350
Oh, okay.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.260
Then Jou-san and OD-san are here, too?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.300
OD-san and Utsutsu 
are in Apartment #2.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.140
Jou-san rarely comes home.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.690
OD-san, Utsutsu-chan!

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.810
I safely completed 
my first combat mission!

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.070
What do you mean "safely"?

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.230
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.490
Does this place have a bathtub?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.820
When are you going to stop 
following me around?

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.780
Oh, but this is my apartment!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.800
Apartment #1!

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.040
Hey, newbie!

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.600
Your luggage is here.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.900
Thanks!

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:02.260
Giraccho, you got here in one piece!

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.390
Honey Karintou

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.050
Oh, what's this place?

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.030
Hey, don't come in without permission.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.310
Oh, I knew you actually liked them.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.190
No, this is just a strategy 
to throw people off!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.420
<i>The Kamoshida Cabinet continues 
to be rocked by bribery allegations.</i>

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.520
<i>In response to recent allegations 
by certain news weeklies that</i>

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.810
I love guys who cook.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.610
Pai-san, you don't cook?

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.070
<i>not only Finance Minister Asada,</i>

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.510
I'm your leader!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:30.490
<i>but also Justice Minister Niigaki 
may have accepted payoffs,</i>

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.330
So stop calling me Pai-san, too!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.910
<i>Prime Minister Kamoshida 
appeared to defend his staff,</i>

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.560
<i>dismissing allegations 
as mere media accusations.</i>

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:36.870
Man, humans are so inferior.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.530
Prime Minister Denies Bribery Allegations

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.530
<i>He has, thus far, rejected any calls 
for his resignation, as unnecessary.</i>

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.500
No wonder they're still under 
surveillance by the rest of the universe!

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:39.750
Opposition to Boycott Diet Deliberations

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.590
Thanks for the meal!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.960
Thanks.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.590
How is it, Leader?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:48.830
Oh, good.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.390
Thank you, as always.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.290
Senpai, this is beautiful!

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.870
R-Really?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:57.900
But...

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.730
I might want to fiddle 
around a bit more.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.250
Done!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:15.980
Here you go!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.710
Come on...

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.960
This is so messed up.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.910
It can't possibly taste good.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:22.850
Delicious!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:24.970
Yay!

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.180
It's good...

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:45.690
Sudden Death of Popular Idol

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.040
<i>Miss Kiritani Noa,</i>

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.140
<i>a member of the popular 
idol group, Goo Goo Pamore,</i>

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.690
<i>has died after jumping 
from her agency's rooftop.</i>

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.750
Man... That's so sad.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.590
<i>Although no suicide 
note has been found,</i>

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.650
I struggle to understand why 
anyone would take their own life.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.460
<i>sources close to the idol believe 
it may have been triggered</i>

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:55.300
<i>by rumors of an affair 
being circulated online...</i>

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:52.580
But...

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.450
maybe she was having 
a really tough time.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:58.620
No, it's because 
she didn't value her life.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:05:59.930
You, too.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.390
What? I'm not gonna die.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:05.010
You don't value people's lives, either.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.090
That's why you can't 
finish off the enemy!

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.650
That's not true.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.320
Hey, newbie.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.640
Oh, I'm Hajime.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.190
Why did you interfere?

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:16.580
I didn't interfere.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.980
It was different!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.580
What was different?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.620
We just shouldn't go 
"Wham!" like Senpai.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.150
That's not what we're about.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.150
Why, you—

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.360
Newbie, you should just follow 
Sugane's orders, for now!

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.130
Boo!

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.650
D-I-Y.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:37.950
Do-It-Y...

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.200
What's Y stand for again?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.610
What are you doing?

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:42.750
Huh? What?

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.340
First, stop drilling!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.860
Oh, oops.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.370
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:49.780
Oh, that's not it.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.800
I forgot to tell everyone 
what time to meet tomorrow.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.970
Tomorrow, at 5:00 PM...

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.970
What does she want to do?

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.340
At the Tachikawa-Kita monorail station.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.140
Guys, meetup's tomorrow 5:00 PM 
at the Tachikawa-Kita monorail station.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:02.710
What's that?

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.650
Oh, it's GALAX.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.230
You don't know about it, Senpai?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:06.820
No.

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.170
I only use my cell phone for calls.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.110
Seriously?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.650
Are you a fossil, Senpai?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.740
Who're you talking to?

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:17.020
Besides, you can use the 
NOTE to make contact!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.440
But that's only with other Gatchaman.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:21.600
Do you have any friends, Senpai?

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.870
GALAX is fun.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.000
That's me.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.190
Aren't my clothes cute?

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:30.880
I designed them, myself.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:33.880
Cute.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.890
They've become sort of popular.

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:35.530
See, she's wearing them, too.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.910
Hi, Rei-chan!

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.620
So it's just playing dress-up.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.340
That's not true.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.040
GALAX is amazing.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.920
It celebrates birthdays, too.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.660
It's just a game.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.550
There are bars and gyms, too.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.710
I got a huge workout last week.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.690
It's a game.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:55.190
You can catch pervs and stalkers, too.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.150
It's not like we only 
interact on GALAX.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:03.340
During the disaster, 
GALAX was a huge help.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.580
Haven't you seen the news, Senpai?

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:08.670
Everyone's been working 
really hard since then.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.870
I went to help out just 
the other day, too.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.560
Did you?

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:16.830
The stars are awesome.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:17.930
I see...

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.010
Decline                Answer

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.010
Mom

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.010
Incoming Call

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.740
Hello.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:23.390
Yep, I'm fine.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.630
I fought.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.060
Huh?

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.390
I didn't get hurt.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.530
I'm fine, okay? But my new home...

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.490
Tachikawa City Hall

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.020
Okay, I'll be leaving now, then.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:35.410
Hey, hey.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:38.670
Jou-san, is it true that 
you're a Tokyo University graduate?

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.920
Maybe. I don't remember 
things that far back.

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.180
Why are you working at City Hall?

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:45.870
You're so efficient.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:48.840
Maybe for the downtime?

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.630
I heard Jou-san was asked

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.520
by the mayor if he'd like 
to become his secretary.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.800
That's a great opportunity!

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.300
I'm not interested.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.200
<i>Major terrorist attack.</i>

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.020
Major Terrorist Attack

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.020
[Drill] Major Terrorist Attack in Chiyoda Ward 
Please evacuate.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.400
<i>Major terrorist attack.</i>

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:03.480
Oh, was the drill today?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.850
It'd be so scary 
if we actually had one.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:08.810
<i>This area may also be 
in danger of a terrorist attack.</i>

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.810
It's actually already happening...

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.520
Tama Monorail

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.280
Senpai!

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:13.990
Hurry!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.950
Chartered Monorail Ride! 
18th 
GALAX
Collage Community 
Meetup

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.950
"GALAX Collage Community Meetup"...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.450
"Collage"?

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.530
What's with this gathering?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.190
Does everyone have 
too much time on their hands?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.600
Are they unemployed?

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.150
Senpai, you haven't done anything yet.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.010
What would I know 
about this collage business?

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:45.020
Anything goes. Just give it a try!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.570
Here, use this maste.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.230
"Maste"?

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.340
Masking tape.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.970
Like this...

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:54.030
And ta-da!

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.430
Isn't your sword pretty?

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.370
C'mon, let's go join everyone.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.280
I'm Kuwabara.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.820
Senpai, he's Baracchi.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:04.750
Hi.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:08.160
<i>This guy isn't just anyone.</i>

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:08.870
<i>Who is he?</i>

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.540
Baracchi's a fire chief.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.430
Huh?

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.910
That man is Nobu-san,

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.450
the mayor of Tachikawa City.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:18.020
Th-The mayor?!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.170
<i>She's right.</i>

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.090
Hey, look.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:20.640
Sir?

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:24.940
These are pictures 
of my daughter growing up.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.020
Nice, right?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:26.600
Right...

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.620
I apologize for not recognizing you.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.900
I am her, I mean 
Ichinose's, classmate—

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:36.370
Oh, your surname is 
Ichinose, Hajime-chan?

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.780
Really?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.190
You don't look like an Ichinose.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.400
Hey!

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.640
You should've told me beforehand

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.160
that they were the fire 
chief and the mayor!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.810
But they're all just normal guys.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.500
They're totally harmless.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:57.870
Who is she,

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.150
really?

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:02.790
You have a great kouhai.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:03.390
Sir?

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:08.460
This meetup began after 
Hajime-chan posted on GALAX.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.740
She said we should make

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.770
collages to send messages 
to the disaster zones.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:14.870
I see.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:18.860
Over time, we just got into collage.

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:22.380
Now, my daughter and I show 
each other our planners.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.620
They say how young'uns 
these days are no good,

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.330
Smile!                            Let's have fun again.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.330
 Together Forever

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.330
Cheer is important 
Cheer is the best!

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:29.830
but you never know until you 
actually get to know one.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.710
Hey, it's not bad.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:41.170
I'm not cut out for this, after all.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.330
It's fine.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.460
Everyone's is different.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.530
I see...

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.470
Man, I hope the whole 
world gets this way, too.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.760
Huh? The world?

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.060
Kind of like this.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:53.690
Lots of different things 
coming together,

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:57.510
but everyone still smiling... 
That'd be great.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.530
Being a civil servant is great, no?

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.810
You can start drinking early.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:18.550
I guess.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:21.290
Hey, you should compete once.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:22.750
You have a chance at winning.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.970
No way, Alan.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.680
There are tons of guys better than me.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.730
You've changed, Jou.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:32.990
Have your dreams changed, too?

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:33.970
Nah.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:35.590
I see.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:36.730
Still the same old:

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.190
world peace.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.990
U-tsu-tsu-chan!

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.110
I'm gloomy .

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.700
You're on GALAX, too, D-san?

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.200
OD.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.060
I heard, Hajime-chan.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.320
You let a MESS go?

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.210
No, that's not it.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.340
Senpai got super ticked off about it!

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.870
"Not it"?

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:05.130
How was it, then?

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:05.950
Well, like...

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.900
There's no point in cutting them down.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.210
Oh, more importantly,

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:12.430
it's like, I haven't really met them!

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.350
Yeah, that's it!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.830
"Met them," huh?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.480
Besides, why are we 
fighting them, anyway?

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:19.940
Whoa!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.740
Are you trying to reject 
the basic premise of Gatchaman?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.500
You're <i>way</i> too fierce!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.700
You're scary, newbie!

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.990
No, really—why?

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.270
"Why"?

00:13:30.270 --> 00:13:31.950
Because that's our duty!

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.290
Oh, you were here, Senpai?

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.360
You don't understand anything.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:38.720
Listen, Gatchaman are—

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.960
Aww, you're starting to sound like him!

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:41.960
Huh?

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.310
Like Pai-Pai!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.990
Who are you calling "Pai-Pai"?!

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:48.500
Pai-Pai, are you on GALAX?

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.690
Don't be ridiculous!

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.440
Of course, I'm all over it!

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.160
Listen up, newbie!

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:56.670
Ha-ji-me.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:57.700
I'm Hajime.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.560
What's with you, too, OD?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:04.150
Listen. Don't bother thinking about 
why you fight or anything else.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.110
Just carry out the mission!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.210
There are casualties every day!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.020
Protect them!

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:10.580
Whose planet is this?

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.130
"Yours, isn't it?!"

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:16.340
Right, you do get it! Good!

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.180
Huh?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:18.830
You!

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.290
What the hell?!

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.230
Oh, isn't it cute?

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:27.120
The NOTE is the lifeblood of Gatchaman!

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:31.700
It is a sacred, physical manifestation 
of each member's soul!

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.270
But see, Hajime-chan,

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:36.350
the NOTE becomes our Achilles' heel 
 when we transform.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.350
If anyone destroys the NOTE, 
then you might die, in the worst case.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.170
Oh, I see.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.320
Hey, I was just about to say that.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.890
The physical materialization 
of each of our souls...

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:47.560
I get it.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.770
That's why our gear and 
weapons are different.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:50.640
That's right!

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:53.700
How dare you paste 
senseless decorations on them?!

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.850
Okay, question:

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.700
Why is it the sword for you, Senpai?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.570
That... I don't know.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.060
I wonder why.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.850
And why is it scissors for me?

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:06.710
But you're a sword kind of guy...

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.700
Like... Straight as an arrow, and stubborn.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.030
Newbie!

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:11.840
Senpai!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.260
Here I was... just listening 
to you, and now this?!

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:15.900
Th-That's <i>my</i> line!

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:17.110
I was the one listening!

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:19.100
Like I said, I'm Hajime!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.730
What? You are the newbie!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.320
Man, that's all you say.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.150
You know the kind 
of person you are, Senpai?

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.860
You just look straight ahead like this,

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.320
and walk in a straight line.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.130
But that means you'll miss 
seeing a lot of things,

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:37.490
like Giraccho, maste,

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.970
and pretty and cute MESS-chan!

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:42.120
If you can't see all 
those kinds of things,

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.710
as a Gatchaman...

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.900
as a person...

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:47.230
you're not <i>at all</i>... you know?

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.330
What's she talking about?

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.550
You!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.480
Like I said, I'm not "you!"

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.680
I'm Hajime!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.290
I'm here.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.230
I've been right here 
next to you, Senpai!

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.100
C-Cut it out already!

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.020
Wings of Six, gather at 
the Spiritual Precipice.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.010
"A bird with sundered 
wings has wandered in."

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:35.470
"The bird is no longer sane."

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.190
What does this mean?

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.140
Hey!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.690
What are you doing?

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.110
You have to be kidding me...

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:57.990
I'm gloomy...

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.490
Oh, hey, JJ.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:11.050
There's something I've 
wanted to ask you.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:25.260
Wow! Amazing!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.790
I think I saw something...

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.530
"Chaos will stand above 
the head of a demon"—

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.690
"The head of a demon" 
sounds pretty interesting.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:43.780
Cut it out.

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:45.400
We're not here to play a game.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:47.110
It really is above the head of a demon!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:51.840
This time, you will not escape.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.100
Let's go!

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:53.710
Amnesia...

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.570
Amnesia Effect!

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.170
Let's go, Senpai!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.470
A-All right.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.020
Go, Bird!

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.830
Relinquish the innocent to us!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.360
Maste?

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.200
Sorry, Senpai!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.130
Grands Ciseaux!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:19.470
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.560
Wings de l'Avenir!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.760
I'm not going to go snippity-snip!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.490
MESS-chan!

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:29.000
Good morning!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:33.630
Wait, no.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.090
Good evening!

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.440
Yeah!

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.970
Nice to meet you!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.470
She's not attacking it?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:55.230
MESS-chan, I've wanted to meet you.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.450
What have you done?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:03.040
I think we've now met!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.380
Hey, it's not safe.

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.120
Stop.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.020
Maybe, but...

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:10.040
Maybe it isn't?

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.040
Huh?

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.770
C'mon, Senpai! Now's the time.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.640
What?

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:20.050
I'm sure it'll tell us now 
where the missing people went.

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:21.550
You...

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:24.970
So cute.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.420
What?

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.780
Don't stare! Damn it!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:35.950
Who are you?

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:44.820
Aww, no way.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:45.950
C'mon.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:49.070
Should I drop fuel?

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.520
Hey, don't stop.

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:51.870
Imma kill you! You're in the way!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.920
Who you talking to, huh?

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:56.630
Outta the way, man.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.200
Let me go!

00:19:58.200 --> 00:19:59.170
Apologize!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.590
Don't get ahead of yourself!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.600
You started it!

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:13.810
Y-Yummyyyy!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:16.520
Crap!

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:17.800
There's blood!

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.180
Get an ambulance!

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:19.440
You make the call.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.100
Get an ambulance!

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.040
I'll try this route.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:24.490
Hey, we have someone injured 
here who fell down the stairs.

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:26.390
It will be fine.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.270
Let's stay calm and deal with this.

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.820
There are three GALAXTERs 
in the vicinity with first aid experience.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:35.500
Yes, stairs in front of the taxi stand 
at Tachikawa Station's North Exit.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.730
I'm a nurse!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.070
I can help.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:37.940
Where do you hurt?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.000
I called the ambulance.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:42.030
Maybe we don't need one?

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.470
GALAX is far more useful.

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:45.840
Maybe.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.070
There's a nurse nearby. 
Looks like it'll be okay.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:48.870
Congratulations.

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.770
The world has been updated.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.730
<i>Maybe I'll go for another round.</i>

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:02.780
It's not heroes who'll update the world.
It's us.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:11.000
Home!

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.060
Welcome back, Rui.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:14.710
Here is my report.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:21.230
There were 228,434 new GALAX 
app installations today.

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:24.430
There are now over two hundred 
million registered users.

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.900
Sounds good.

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:33.730
87.5% of them are active users, 
up 0.5% from yesterday.

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.100
But there's still a long way to go.

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:40.480
Man, I'm starving.
